      "summary": ": Today at Cardrona Alpine Resort 25 Aug 2026 – Cardrona is open after 2–5cm of heavy wet snow this morning, with very strong westerly winds easing but still affecting lift operations. Conditions are currently 2°C with winds around 37km/h and gusts to 69km/h. Fresh cord has been laid on the groomed trails, while the upper mountain has drier snow and lower areas remain very soft and wet. Snow showers are possible this afternoon. Kindy Conveyor, Learner Conveyors, Valley View, Captains Express and T-Bar are open. McDougall’s Chondola, Whitestar Express and Soho Express are on wind hold, with Whitestar added to the hold at 1:50pm; Willow’s Quad and Wells Pipe Platter are closed. McDougall’s is operating chairs only today, with no gondola or sightseeing service. Current terrain includes Learners Slope, Main Basin, Captains, Ski Touring Access, Arcadia Chutes and Summit, while Soho and Mt Cardrona are on hold and Little Willows and Big Willows are closed. The access roads are chain-free but chains must be carried, with an active road-hazard advisory. Four of six carparks are open, with Carparks A and B full and C, The Yard, Valley View and The Pines available. Five of nine listed park areas are open. The Cardrona National Junior Champs GS race has been cancelled today, and there will be no sightseeing.",
