      "summary": ": Today at Treble Cone 25 Aug 2026 – Treble Cone is open with 9cm of estimated new snow overnight, although the snow is heavy and wet and lower elevations are becoming sticky as precipitation changes to rain at the base. Winds are still gusting through The Saddle but are easing overall, with the upper mountain offering the best skiing and riding. Fresh cord has been laid across the groomers, with some wind-blown snow covering the groomed surface. Home Basin Express and Beginner Platter are open, while Saddle Quad remains on wind hold. Home Basin, Powder Bowl and Matukituki Basin are open, with Saddle Basin and Summit Slopes on hold and Motatapu Chutes and Sundance closed. Groomed terrain including Main Street, Upper Skite, Saddle Track, Pete's Treat, Raffils Run, High Street, Bullet and Saddle Back is open, while operations remain subject to wind updates. The access road is chain-free but all vehicles must carry chains, with an active road-hazard advisory in place. Two of three carparks are open, with Carpark 1 full and Carparks 2 and 3 available. Backcountry Access and Skinning Access are open. The resort is also advising guests to monitor updates through the day as winds continue to affect the Saddle.",
